This MIT license applies to the original DAO source code. Third-party
software and adapted routines retain their respective rights and terms:

  - Cloudy (Gary J. Ferland and collaborators) is licensed under the zlib
    license <https://opensource.org/licenses/Zlib> and must be obtained
    separately from <https://gitlab.nublado.org/cloudy/cloudy>. DAO links to
    an unmodified Cloudy installation and extracts atomic data, emissivities,
    and opacities through its interfaces for DAO's transfer calculation.
    DAO does not distribute the Cloudy library or source distribution.

  - DAO links to the XSPEC model library (libXSFunctions) supplied with
    HEASoft to evaluate the nthcomp and compTT incident continua. This library
    is installed separately and retains its upstream terms; it is not
    distributed with DAO. See
    <https://heasarc.gsfc.nasa.gov/docs/software/heasoft/>.

  - The Compton redistribution and cross-section routines in
    source/compton_kernel.cpp and source/compton_cross_section.cpp include
    C++ ports of Fortran routines by Jerzy Madej, a co-author of the DAO
    paper. These adaptations of his routines are included with his permission.
    Original code: <https://www.astrouw.edu.pl/~jm/software.html>.
    If you use these routines, please cite:
        Madej J., Rozanska A., Majczyna A., Nalezyta M., 2017,
        MNRAS, 469, 2032
        <https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/2017MNRAS.469.2032M>.
